# .plan — tarang@atlas
# public notes from the product workstation

2026  shipped Locus as a real control and evidence layer for coding
            agents. the benchmark reports what it measures and refuses to
            pretend localization recall equals autonomous task success.

2026  built Tickmark around one idea: a human correction should become
            a tested rule, not another permanent paragraph in a prompt.

2026  rebuilt the profile as a live tmux machine. visitors can inspect
            the work, open the products, and break the disk by filing issues.
            this is more entertaining than another grid of badges.

